[module:SYSCTL][policy:kernel_exec_shield_enable][description]=Buffer overflow protection.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:kernel_dmesg_restrict][description]=Restricts access to dmesg output for unprivileged users.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:fs_file_max_limit][description]=Sets the maximum number of open files in the system. A value that is too low can limit high-load services and reduce performance under load.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:fs_protected_hardlinks][description]=Enables protection against unsafe hardlinks.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ipv4_default_accept_redirects_disable][description]=Prevents accepting IPv4 redirects on new interfaces by default.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ipv4_default_rp_filter_enable][description]=Enables IPv4 reverse path filtering on new interfaces by default. On complex routed or multi-homed systems it may affect network performance and traffic availability.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ipv4_default_send_redirects_disable][description]=Prevents sending IPv4 redirects on new interfaces by default.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ipv6_all_accept_redirects_disable][description]=Prevents accepting IPv6 redirects on all interfaces.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ipv6_default_accept_redirects_disable][description]=Prevents accepting IPv6 redirects on new interfaces by default.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ipv6_packet_forwarding_disable][description]=Disables IPv6 packet forwarding.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:kernel_kptr_restrict][description]=Restricts kernel pointer exposure in /proc and dmesg.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:fs_nr_open_limit][description]=Sets the maximum number of file descriptors per process. A value that is too low can limit applications with many connections or open files.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ipv4_packet_forwarding_disable][description]=Disables IPv4 packet forwarding.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:kernel_perf_event_paranoid][description]=Restricts access to perf_event. It may make performance profiling and diagnostics harder for unprivileged users.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:fs_protected_symlinks][description]=Enables protection against unsafe symlinks.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:kernel_pid_max_limit][description]=Sets the maximum number of PIDs in the system. A value that is too low can limit systems with many processes and services.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ptrace_proc_restriction][description]=Restricts ptrace for unprivileged processes.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:kernel_randomize_va_space][description]=Enables ASLR for process address spaces. Performance impact is usually minimal, but some workloads may see a small process startup overhead.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ipv4_all_accept_redirects_disable][description]=Prevents accepting IPv4 redirects on all interfaces.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ipv4_all_rp_filter_enable][description]=Enables IPv4 reverse path filtering on all interfaces. On complex routed or multi-homed systems it may affect network performance and traffic availability.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:ipv4_all_send_redirects_disable][description]=Prevents sending IPv4 redirects on all interfaces.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:fs_suid_dump_disable][description]=Prevents core dump creation for SUID/SGID processes.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:tcp_syncookies_enable][description]=Enables SYN cookies for SYN flood protection.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:tcp_keepalive_time][description]=Sets the time before a TCP connection sends keepalive probes. Overly aggressive values can increase network and CPU load on hosts with many connections.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:tcp_max_syn_backlog][description]=Sets the maximum SYN backlog queue size. A value that is too low can hurt performance and availability during bursts of incoming connections.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:tcp_synack_retries][description]=Sets the number of SYN-ACK retries. Values that are too low can reduce availability on unstable networks, while values that are too high keep connection resources allocated longer.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:tcp_fin_timeout][description]=Sets the FIN timeout for TCP connections. Values that are too high keep resources occupied longer, while values that are too low can affect compatibility and connection stability.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:kernel_threads_max_limit][description]=Sets the maximum number of threads in the system. A value that is too low can limit multithreaded applications and large numbers of services.
[module:SYSCTL][policy:user_namespace_restriction][description]=Restricts creation of user namespaces by unprivileged users.

